<!--
  The hardware video codecs of the host, which the Virtio video device presents
  as V4L2 stateful encoders and decoders and external/v4l2_codec2 exposes
  through Codec2. The product installs this file as /vendor/etc/media_codecs_c2.xml,
  the file the Codec2 codec list reads beside media_codecs.xml. It is the
  product's one vendor codec list, so it also carries the updates (update="true")
  to the limits of the software decoders.

  The decoders are HEVC (Main and Main 10) and H.264, the formats the host
  decodes in hardware. The component takes the profiles and levels from the
  device and lists the High tier of every HEVC level the device lists; this file
  states what MediaCodecInfo cannot learn from the component. CTS wants the width
  and height ranges of a decoder to be the same, and the component limits a
  stream to 4096x4096 samples. It asks every hardware decoder for adaptive
  playback and for dynamic colour aspects, which the component implements: it
  follows a change of resolution and reads the colour of each coded video
  sequence.

  The sizes, bitrates and levels of the encoders follow the encoder component,
  which offers AVC up to level 5.2 and HEVC Main up to the highest level the
  device lists. The component derives the bitrate modes and the QP bounds from
  the device's controls, and these entries state what the Virtio video encoder
  publishes for a VideoToolbox hardware encoder: VBR, CBR and constant quality.

  The performance points and measured frame rates are what the codecs sustain
  through the frame copy between the guest and the host, which grows with the
  picture. For the encoders, each lower bound is about four fifths of the
  slowest rate the CTS encoder performance test measured for the size and each
  upper bound a tenth above the fastest, so 4K HEVC encoding is published below
  30 frames per second. For the decoders, a performance point's lower bound is
  four fifths of the slowest rate the CTS decoder performance test achieved at
  its size, so that CTS tests every clip the point covers at 30 frames per
  second, and its upper bound is the rate the decoder keeps up with at that
  size. The measured frame rates of a decoder are the range the CTS decoder
  test observes: the upper bound is a tenth above the fastest rate of a quiet
  host and the lower bound about half of the slowest, because the decode rate
  swings with the load of the host.

  The encoders start at 64x64 pixels and 20 kbit/s. VideoToolbox emits streams
  for smaller pictures, but they decode to something far from the source: CTS
  VideoEncoderMinMaxTest measures a PSNR under its 20 dB threshold at every size
  with a side of 48 pixels or fewer, and passes at 64. At 64x64 an HEVC stream
  with inter frames holds the 20 dB only from about 10 kbit/s, so the bitrate
  range starts at twice that. The component clamps its picture size and bitrate
  to the same bounds, so the two agree.

  A decoder keeps a pool of decoded pictures in the guest's memory that grows
  with the picture: one 4K stream costs about 0.9 GiB of the guest's 8 GiB.
  Four concurrent decoders at the largest size fit; eight do not, and
  Android's low memory killer ends the process, so the decoders state four
  concurrent instances (ro.vendor.v4l2_codec2.decode_concurrent_instances) and
  the encoders, whose buffers stay on the host, eight.

  The software decoders of the swcodec APEX advertise less than they decode: VP9
  stops at 2048x2048 and HEVC at 2,000,000 8x8 blocks per second, which is 1080p
  at 60 frames per second. Both decode 3840x2160 correctly, so the product states
  the capability the Mainline CTS asks of some component of every device. This
  vendor file is parsed after the APEX's and updates their entries
  (update="true"); the values not named here stay. Verified by
  tools/verify-target-files.py: HEVC at 3840x2160 and 30 frames per second
  (129,600 blocks, 3,888,000 per second) and VP9 at 3840x2160 (32,400 16x16
  blocks) must be inside the limits.
-->
<MediaCodecs>
    <Decoders>
        <MediaCodec name="c2.v4l2.hevc.decoder" type="video/hevc">
            <Limit name="size" min="64x64" max="4096x4096" />
            <Limit name="alignment" value="2x2" />
            <Limit name="block-size" value="16x16" />
            <Limit name="block-count" range="1-65536" />
            <Limit name="blocks-per-second" range="1-4147200" />
            <Limit name="frame-rate" range="1-240" />
            <Limit name="bitrate" range="1-240000000" />
            <Limit name="concurrent-instances" max="4" />
            <Limit name="performance-point-3840x2160" range="49-55" />
            <Limit name="performance-point-1920x1080" range="131-150" />
            <Limit name="performance-point-1280x720" range="133-155" />
            <Limit name="performance-point-720x480" range="202-235" />
            <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-352x288" range="190-445" />
            <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-640x360" range="210-385" />
            <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-720x480" range="202-380" />
            <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-1280x720" range="133-295" />
            <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-1920x1080" range="131-203" />
            <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-3840x2160" range="49-62" />
            <Feature name="adaptive-playback" />
            <Feature name="dynamic-color-aspects" />
        </MediaCodec>
        <MediaCodec name="c2.v4l2.avc.decoder" type="video/avc">
            <Limit name="size" min="64x64" max="4096x4096" />
            <Limit name="alignment" value="2x2" />
            <Limit name="block-size" value="16x16" />
            <Limit name="block-count" range="1-65536" />
            <Limit name="blocks-per-second" range="1-2211840" />
            <Limit name="frame-rate" range="1-240" />
            <Limit name="bitrate" range="1-240000000" />
            <Limit name="concurrent-instances" max="4" />
            <Limit name="performance-point-3840x2160" range="48-55" />
            <Limit name="performance-point-1920x1080" range="118-140" />
            <Limit name="performance-point-1280x720" range="153-170" />
            <Limit name="performance-point-720x480" range="166-185" />
            <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-320x240" range="210-430" />
            <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-720x480" range="166-365" />
            <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-1280x720" range="153-253" />
            <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-1920x1080" range="118-163" />
            <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-3840x2160" range="48-73" />
            <Feature name="adaptive-playback" />
            <Feature name="dynamic-color-aspects" />
        </MediaCodec>
        <!-- HEVC Main tier level 5.2, which the software decoder already reports:
             4096x2176 at 60 frames per second is 1,069,547,520 luma samples per
             second. -->
        <MediaCodec name="c2.android.hevc.decoder" type="video/hevc" update="true">
            <Limit name="blocks-per-second" range="1-16711680" />
        </MediaCodec>
        <MediaCodec name="c2.android.vp9.decoder" type="video/x-vnd.on2.vp9" update="true">
            <Limit name="size" min="2x2" max="4096x4096" />
            <Limit name="block-count" range="1-65536" />
            <Limit name="blocks-per-second" range="1-2000000" />
        </MediaCodec>
    </Decoders>
    <Encoders>
        <MediaCodec name="c2.v4l2.avc.encoder" type="video/avc">
            <Limit name="size" min="64x64" max="4096x4096" />
            <Limit name="alignment" value="2x2" />
            <Limit name="block-size" value="16x16" />
            <Limit name="block-count" range="1-36864" />
            <Limit name="blocks-per-second" range="1-2073600" />
            <Limit name="frame-rate" range="1-240" />
            <Limit name="bitrate" range="20000-240000000" />
            <Limit name="quality" range="1-100" default="50" />
            <Limit name="concurrent-instances" max="8" />
            <Limit name="performance-point-1920x1080" range="30-45" />
            <Limit name="performance-point-1280x720" range="60-86" />
            <Limit name="performance-point-720x480" range="105-170" />
            <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-320x240" range="200-295" />
            <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-720x480" range="105-170" />
            <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-1280x720" range="60-86" />
            <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-1920x1080" range="31-45" />
            <Feature name="bitrate-modes" value="VBR,CBR,CQ" />
            <Feature name="qp-bounds" />
        </MediaCodec>
        <MediaCodec name="c2.v4l2.hevc.encoder" type="video/hevc">
            <Limit name="size" min="64x64" max="4096x4096" />
            <Limit name="alignment" value="2x2" />
            <Limit name="block-size" value="16x16" />
            <Limit name="block-count" range="1-65536" />
            <Limit name="blocks-per-second" range="1-4177920" />
            <Limit name="frame-rate" range="1-240" />
            <Limit name="bitrate" range="20000-60000000" />
            <Limit name="quality" range="1-100" default="50" />
            <Limit name="concurrent-instances" max="8" />
            <Limit name="performance-point-3840x2160" range="8-13" />
            <Limit name="performance-point-1920x1080" range="30-45" />
            <Limit name="performance-point-1280x720" range="60-90" />
            <Limit name="performance-point-720x480" range="115-170" />
            <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-320x240" range="200-320" />
            <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-720x480" range="115-170" />
            <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-1280x720" range="60-90" />
            <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-1920x1080" range="31-45" />
            <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-3840x2160" range="8-13" />
            <Feature name="bitrate-modes" value="VBR,CBR,CQ" />
            <Feature name="qp-bounds" />
        </MediaCodec>
    </Encoders>
</MediaCodecs>
